{:event/id "6406ff1c-d114-4032-a409-bf468f2820b2" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:7e538f44-5ece-4da7-8c25-40bfee006a17" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["7e538f44-5ece-4da7-8c25-40bfee006a17"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:7e538f44-5ece-4da7-8c25-40bfee006a17" :event/at "2026-09-13T14:03:28Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/translation-dispatch-fences-stable-key-with-attempt-generation :finding/shapes #{:state-machine :reservation :identity :reconciliation} :finding/current-name "dispatch key + dispatch attempt id + attempt-binding CAS" :finding/candidate-name "AttemptFencedClaim<Key,Attempt>" :finding/claim "One durable dispatch key identifies the logical translation request while each retry carries a fresh attempt id. Store mutation predicates compare the exact immutable attempt binding, and replacement clears stale batch/detail state; delayed bind, failure, or completion from an earlier attempt therefore loses instead of mutating its replacement. This is a durable ABA fence over a logical claim, not a SeenSet and not merely the process-local RetryableDedupGate."}}
{:event/id "97bcd59e-f85e-45be-9a40-9ac29ac4559c" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:7e538f44-5ece-4da7-8c25-40bfee006a17" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["6406ff1c-d114-4032-a409-bf468f2820b2"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:7e538f44-5ece-4da7-8c25-40bfee006a17" :event/at "2026-09-13T14:03:28Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/translation-receipts-are-provisional-until-attempt-settlement :finding/shapes #{:fact :projection :visibility :recovery} :finding/current-name "completion owner + record-translation! + receipt-visible-for-dispatch? + finish-dispatch-completion!" :finding/candidate-name "ReceiptVisibilityFence<Attempt,Fact>" :finding/claim "Translation completion first claims exclusive ownership for the exact attempt, persists the immutable receipt, then marks that same attempt completed. Attempt-bound receipts are deliberately invisible to completed-evidence readers until the matching dispatch row is completed, so a crash after receipt persistence does not expose provisional evidence; an equal retry resumes the owner and completes exactly once. Durable existence and admissible visibility are therefore separate laws."}}
